CAT = "s24Registration"; SEG = "REG"
Q = [
('A member firm wants to close one of its branch offices. In the CRD system it updates the branch record by filing:',
 'Form BR', ['Form BD', 'Form BDW', 'Form U5'],
 'Form BR is the uniform branch office registration form used to register, amend and close branch offices in CRD. Form BD registers the broker-dealer itself, Form BDW withdraws that registration and Form U5 terminates an individual.'),
('A broker-dealer that is leaving the securities business ends its SEC, SRO and state registrations by filing:',
 'Form BDW', ['Form BR', 'Form ADV-W', 'Form U5'],
 'Form BDW is the uniform request for broker-dealer withdrawal (SEC Rule 15b6-1). Form ADV-W withdraws an investment adviser, not a broker-dealer.'),
('When a firm files a Form U5 on a departing representative, the FINRA By-Laws also require the firm to:',
 'Give the person a copy of the filing', ['Get the person to sign the form first', 'Send a copy to each of the person\'s customers', 'File a duplicate with the SEC'],
 'Article V, Section 3 of the FINRA By-Laws requires the member to give the terminated person a copy of the notice of termination (Form U5) at the same time it is filed.'),
('A firm wants a representative to act as a principal for up to 120 calendar days before passing the Series 24. The representative must have at least:',
 '18 months of experience as a representative in the past five years', ['12 months of experience as a representative in the past three years', 'Three years of experience as a branch manager', 'Five years of experience with this firm'],
 'Rule 1210.04 allows a 120-day principal designation only for a person with at least 18 months of experience functioning as a registered representative within the five years before the designation, who meets all other prerequisites.'),
('A member firm with more than one associated person must generally have at least how many officers or partners registered as General Securities Principals?',
 'Two', ['One', 'Three', 'Four'],
 'Rule 1210.01 requires a member with more than one associated person to have at least two officers or partners registered as principals, subject to limited-scope categories and waivers under the Rule 9600 Series.'),
('Which fact would make an applicant subject to statutory disqualification?',
 'A felony conviction eight years ago', ['A personal bankruptcy six years ago', 'A customer complaint that was denied', 'A speeding ticket last month'],
 'Under Exchange Act Section 3(a)(39) and the FINRA By-Laws, a felony conviction within the past 10 years is a statutory disqualification. A bankruptcy or a denied complaint is disclosed on Form U4 but is not a disqualification.'),
('Under Rule 3110(e), a firm must verify the information on a new hire\'s Form U4 by, at a minimum, searching reasonably available public records within:',
 '30 calendar days after the Form U4 is filed', ['10 business days before the person starts', '60 days after the first trade', '6 months after the hire date'],
 'Rule 3110(e) requires written procedures to verify the accuracy and completeness of Form U4 no later than 30 calendar days after it is filed, including a search of reasonably available public records.'),
('A firm hires a person who was registered at another member firm. Rule 3110(e) requires the firm to review the person\'s most recent Form U5 within:',
 '60 days of filing the registration application', ['5 business days of the start date', '30 days before making an offer', '1 year of the hire'],
 'Under Rule 3110(e), when the applicant was previously registered, the member must review the most recent Form U5 within 60 days of filing the application for registration.'),
('A representative misses the deadline for the Continuing Education Regulatory Element. Until it is completed, the representative:',
 'Is CE inactive and may not do registered business', ['May keep working but owes FINRA a late fee', 'Must retake the qualification exam', 'Loses all trail commissions on past sales'],
 'Under Rule 1240(a), a person who does not complete the Regulatory Element by the deadline is CE inactive: no registered activity and no new transaction-based pay. Trailing commissions on earlier sales may continue unless the firm forbids them.'),
('A former principal left the industry three years ago and did not elect the Maintaining Qualifications Program. To register as a principal again, the person must:',
 'Pass the principal exam again', ['Only finish the current Regulatory Element', 'File a new Form BR for the office', 'Wait out a 180-day cooling-off period'],
 'Rule 1210.08 treats a principal qualification as lapsed after two years out of registration. Only a person who maintained the qualification under Rule 1240(c) avoids retaking the exam.'),
('Under FINRA\'s taping rule (Rule 3170), a firm must tape its registered persons\' calls with existing and potential customers when:',
 'Enough of its registered persons came from disciplined firms', ['It opens a call center for retail clients', 'It receives five complaints in one year', 'It begins selling variable annuities'],
 'Rule 3170 makes a firm a taping firm when the share of its registered persons who were associated with disciplined firms in the past three years reaches the rule\'s thresholds. Taping firms must record and review those calls for three years.'),
('SEC Rule 15a-6 lets a foreign broker-dealer that is not registered in the United States:',
 'Deal with major U.S. institutional investors through a registered U.S. broker-dealer', ['Open accounts for U.S. retail customers by mail', 'Underwrite U.S. public offerings without limit', 'Act as a market maker on a U.S. exchange'],
 'Rule 15a-6 exempts foreign broker-dealers that, among other things, contact major U.S. institutional investors and U.S. institutional investors through a registered U.S. broker-dealer that effects the trades and keeps the records.'),
]
